+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static homepage. No build step or dependencies are required.
+
+## SMS verification
+
+The page defaults to an explicitly labeled interactive demo. No SMS is sent and no authentication happens. Enter a mobile number including its country code and use `123456` to preview the Rewards or ordering flow. Demo codes expire after five minutes and allow five attempts; resend has a 30-second cooldown.
+
+To enable real authentication, add this to the HTML head:
+
+```html
+<meta name="auth-api-base" content="/api/auth">
+```
+
+Implement same-origin HTTPS endpoints:
+
+- `POST /api/auth/send-code`: accepts JSON `{ "phone": "+12025550123", "intent": "rewards" }` (`intent` can also be `order`). Sends an SMS and returns `{ "challengeId": "opaque-server-generated-id" }`.
+- `POST /api/auth/verify-code`: accepts `{ "challengeId": "...", "code": "012345", "intent": "rewards" }`. Verify the code on the server, establish an authenticated session via a Secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookie, and return `{ "verified": true }` only on success. The client then navigates to `/rewards` or `/order-online`.
+
+Bind challenges to phone numbers and sessions, generate unpredictable codes, enforce expiry, single use, resend and attempt limits server-side, invalidate old codes when resending, and check request Origin for CSRF protection. Never trust the client’s validation or intent as authorization. Do not log phone numbers or codes. Production request failures never fall back to demo verification.
+
+The SMS must end with the actual page host and code, with no scheme, port, path, signature, or trailing lines:
+
+```text
+Your Daily Grind verification code is 012345.
+
+@your-production-host.example #012345
+```
+
+On compatible devices, WebOTP requests user consent to extract an origin-bound code and submits it through the normal validated form handler. The receiver starts when the code-entry step becomes active and is cancelled on submit, resend, phone/intent changes, navigation, or a two-minute timeout. Other browsers retain system `one-time-code` autofill and manual/paste input in one accessible text field. Production requires HTTPS. WebOTP is never requested in demo mode.
+
+## Validation
+
+No development or preview servers are needed. JavaScript can be syntax-checked with `node --check verification.js`. No browser verification was performed.
